<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Badr al-Jamali</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1094">1094</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Badr al-Jamali was an Armenian commander who became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a> in 1073 after being summoned to restore order during a severe crisis. He reorganised the army and administration and rebuilt the walls and gates of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bab-al-futuh">Bab al-Futuh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bab-al-nasr">Bab al-Nasr</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bab-zuwayla">Bab Zuwayla</a>. His rule began a period in which military viziers held real power over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/badr-al-jamali.jpg" alt="Badr al-Jamali" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Md iet · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juyushi_Mosque,Cairo_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
